  "body": "4.22.0 added the cache columns but **nothing populated them for the providers most people actually use**. PATCH `4.22.0` → `4.22.1`.\n\n## Why it showed 0\n\nMy capture only understood Anthropic-shaped fields (`cache_read_input_tokens`). OpenAI-compatible upstreams report cache hits under `usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`, and the shared `_anthropic_usage_fields` returned `{}` — so NVIDIA NIM, OpenRouter, Novita and every other OpenAI-shaped provider reported 0 cached and 0.0% regardless of what the upstream said.\n\n**Confirmed with a live NVIDIA NIM call**, not assumed:\n\n```json\n{\"prompt_tokens\": 1243, \"completion_tokens\": 2,\n \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\"audio_tokens\": null, \"cached_tokens\": 32}}\n```\n\nNIM does report caching. We were dropping it.\n\nThe lookup now lives in the shared OpenAI-chat base so the whole family gains it at once. DeepSeek keeps its override — it uses non-standard `prompt_cache_hit_tokens`/`prompt_cache_miss_tokens`.\n\n## The rate maths was also wrong\n\n`prompt_tokens` **already includes** the cached tokens (and DeepSeek's hit + miss likewise sum to the prompt total). 4.22.0 treated `tokens_in` as an *uncached* figure and added cache reads on top — counting them twice and understating the rate.\n\nCorrected:\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Input (uncached) | `tokens_in - cache_read` |\n| Cache hit rate | `cache_read / tokens_in` |\n\nAgainst the sample above: **1211 uncached, 2.6%** — matching the upstream.\n\n## Verification\n\nHelper checked against the real NIM numbers plus boundaries:\n\n```\nNIM real sample -> uncached 1211 | hit 2.6%\nno cache        -> uncached 500  | hit 0.0%\nfully cached    -> uncached 0    | hit 100.0%\nno data         -> uncached 0    | hit —\n```\n\nNew tests cover the dict and SDK-object shapes, and assert a provider that doesn't report caching yields **no fields at all** rather than a fabricated zero — so \"unsupported\" stays distinguishable from \"measured zero\".\n\nFull suite passes except the 14 failures that also fail on unmodified `main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nOnly new traffic populates this. Existing rows keep `NULL`, so the dashboard will show a low overall hit rate until history turns over — the totals mix pre- and post-upgrade requests.\n\nCache *writes* remain unpopulated for OpenAI-shaped providers: the OpenAI schema has no cache-creation counter, so that card stays 0 for NIM. It's only meaningful for Anthropic-shaped and DeepSeek upstreams.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
