    "message": "fix(analytics): read prompt cache hits from OpenAI-compatible providers\n\n4.22.0 added the cache columns but nothing populated them for the providers\nmost people actually use. The capture only understood Anthropic-shaped fields,\nand OpenAI-compatible upstreams report cache hits under\nusage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens instead. The base\n_anthropic_usage_fields returned an empty dict, so NVIDIA NIM, OpenRouter,\nNovita and every other OpenAI-shaped provider reported 0 cached and a 0.0% hit\nrate no matter what the upstream actually said.\n\nConfirmed against a live NVIDIA NIM call rather than assumed:\n\n    {\"prompt_tokens\": 1243, \"completion_tokens\": 2,\n     \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\"audio_tokens\": null, \"cached_tokens\": 32}}\n\nThe lookup now lives in the shared OpenAI-chat base, so the whole family gains\nit at once instead of each provider repeating it -- DeepSeek keeps its own\noverride because it uses non-standard prompt_cache_hit/miss fields.\n\nThe rate maths was also wrong. prompt_tokens already includes the cached\ntokens, and DeepSeek's hit + miss likewise sum to the prompt total, so treating\ntokens_in as an uncached figure and adding cache reads on top counted them\ntwice and understated the rate. The uncached figure is now the remainder\n(tokens_in - cache_read) and the hit rate divides by tokens_in. Against the\nsample above that reads 1211 uncached and 2.6%, matching the upstream.\n\nVerified: helper output checked against the real NIM numbers, plus the boundary\ncases (no cache 0.0%, fully cached 100.0%, no data an em dash). New tests cover\nthe dict and SDK-object shapes and assert that a provider which does not report\ncaching yields no fields at all rather than a fabricated zero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
